  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2xc6e3yec2m",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Not that AI discourse has ever been great, but \"of course LLMs are good at math\" both misses that \"good at math\" is an *slight* understatement in the context of solving the Reimann Hypothesis & also ignores the fact that LLMs were not actually \"good at math\" until very recent breakthroughs.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2xc6e3yec2m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T04:29:03.646Z",
      "likes": 255,
      "replies": 10,
      "reposts": 19,
      "score": 7.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.5,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 15.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2x4fwduu22m",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Yes, it is reasonable to expect AI models struggle more with unverifiable domains, but I do think it is worth noting that we also see very large gains in domains without automatic verification as well\n\nHere are humans evaluations of AI in writing, business problems, design, and doing freelance tasks",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2x4fwduu22m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T02:45:55.208Z",
      "likes": 89,
      "replies": 6,
      "reposts": 5,
      "score": 6.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 17
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2yixn4gps2g",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Walmart seems determined not to make the same mistake with agentic commerce that it did with ecommerce. While Amazon is blocking agents, Walmart is embracing them - quite a reversal.\n\nAnd the new data from Stripe suggests agentic shopping may actually be kicking off & is suprisingly sticky.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2yixn4gps2g",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T16:03:14.146Z",
      "likes": 68,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 4,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 3.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2yruspowk2r",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "A likely explanation is that students with very similar responses used an LLM to assist with this assignment. So the reason I am pointing this out is that I hope it will be a useful lesson to you on the limitations of LLMs - particularly what we learned in class about homogenization.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3n2yruspowk2r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T18:42:43.034Z",
      "likes": 21,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2wyrdmla22n",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "I don't hesitate to block. undisclosed bots. People that are clearly using AI to write posts will probably be blocked too. \n\nI'm on social media to interact with people. The \"social\" part. If I want to talk to an AI, I have Claude and ChatGPT apps for that. \n\nYou're just wasting my time, otherwise.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2wyrdmla22n",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T01:40:43.257Z",
      "likes": 24,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 18.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2ysbebic22r",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "Additionally, in this course you are permitted to use AI as long as you disclose. So if this was the case for you, it is worth considering why you decided not to do so. When you do not want others to know you use AI, you could potentially learn something from some self reflection about why that is.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3n2ysbebic22r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T18:49:44.097Z",
      "likes": 16,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 5.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.3,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 0.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2yryorh5s2r",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "And of course when we take this issue at the scale of society, frequent uses of AI in this way and subsequent impacts on human creativity could have a broad harmful homogenizing impact.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3n2yryorh5s2r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T18:44:53.116Z",
      "likes": 15,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 5.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.3,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2ypg4mwgc2w",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "This is nonsense. AI did 25 years of math research in 3 months? What if AI did 25 years of AI research in 3 months? Do we get rogue AI? No. AI research is, in part, about safe and reliable systems. 25 years of that in 3 months gives really safe and reliable AI. The most not-going-rogue AI ever.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2ypg4mwgc2w",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T17:58:42.622Z",
      "likes": 10,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.1,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2vshrz37226",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "The Alignment Research Center is super sketch. A handful of people who started a charitable organization whose “benefit” to society is saving humanity from extinction by AI. Funded almost exclusively by likeminded philanthropists, like Sam Bankman-Fried.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2vshrz37226",
